Binaural HRIR tables (sadie2_ku100_*.bin)

Derived from the SADIE II Database, subject D1 (Neumann KU100 dummy head).
Copyright 2018, University of York. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see SADIE-II-LICENSE.txt).

Source: https://zenodo.org/records/12092466 (D1_HRIR_SOFA.zip)
Reference: C. Armstrong, L. Thresh, D. Murphy, G. Kearney, "A Perceptual Evaluation of
Individual and Non-Individual HRTFs: A Case Study of the SADIE II Database",
Applied Sciences 8(11), 2029 (2018). doi:10.3390/app8112029

Modifications (tools/make_hrir.py): only the 0-degree-elevation ring is kept and
re-indexed clockwise; one global onset delay is removed; responses are cut or
zero-padded to 256 taps at 48 kHz (scaled with the sample rate; the measured
responses are shorter, so the script's fade-out falls on the padding); the 88.2,
176.4 and 192 kHz tables are resampled from the 44.1 and 96 kHz measurements; a
per-ear gain equalises the ear microphones, and each table is scaled so the front
direction matches the stereo pan level at centre.
